# Paths here need one approving review from a listed owner before a pull request into bleeding-edge
# merges. Everything NOT listed needs no review, only the guard's checks. Docs/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md.
#
# Any ONE listed owner's approval is enough. GitHub never lets a PR's author approve it, so a change
# authored by an owner still needs one of the others. The LAST matching line wins, so a later, narrower
# line replaces an earlier one's owners rather than adding to them.
#
# Agent sessions still act on GitHub as Shombith03, so an approval from that account does not yet prove a
# human read the change; Docs/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md section 4 moves agents to their own account, which
# fixes that. Never list the agent account here: its approval would then count.
#
# This only blocks a merge while the "Protect trunks" ruleset requires review from Code Owners.

